Day 21: Learning to Trust | Tuesday of the Third Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“Trust in the Lord with all your heart.”
Not the easy parts.
Not the certain parts.
All of it.

Welcome to Day 21 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you into one of the most vulnerable and beautiful movements of the spiritual life: trust — the kind that grows slowly, honestly, and through small acts of surrender.

This spoken‑word devotional meets you in the places where the path feels unclear, where questions feel heavy, and where the future feels uncertain. It reminds you that trust is not pretending you’re not afraid — it’s bringing your fear to God and letting Him hold it with you.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why trust grows slowly, not instantly

How God invites you to trust with your whole heart — even the anxious parts

Why trust is choosing God when you can’t see the next step

A prayer to surrender your fears and lean into God’s wisdom

A simple daily activity: “Jesus, I trust in You” spoken slowly, three times

If this reflection blesses you, consider continuing the journey through all 40 days of Lent.

Peace be with you.

